// Privilege escalation via sudo
//
// Surfaces every command run through sudo. On Azure Ubuntu images the
// azureuser account has passwordless sudo, so each escalation lands in
// the authpriv facility as a "COMMAND=" line.
//
// Note: sudo events are identified by ProcessName, not by the text of the
// message. Filtering SyslogMessage for "sudo" returns nothing, because the
// word "sudo" does not appear in the message body. Filter on ProcessName
// and search the body for the command that was run.

Syslog
| where ProcessName == "sudo"
| where SyslogMessage has "COMMAND"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, ProcessName, SyslogMessage
| order by TimeGenerated desc
